        "id": 6163,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-08-15T21:47:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think I read that Personal Messages are a known issue with the forums currently, but I wanted to recount my personal experience of a few minutes ago in case something can be done to improve it.</p><p>1) Nowhere on the site can I find info about any Personal Messages I may or may not have.&nbsp; I think I read that a tab should be displayed for me that's not currently being displayed, so that's a known issue.</p><p>2) I got an email on my iPhone saying that I've got a new PM, so that's good news that notifications are working.&nbsp; Since I can't seem to get to them on my PC, I'll just hit the link in the notification email.</p><p>3) It takes me to my profile page that says \"access denied\".&nbsp; I'm not logged in on my iPhone, so I do that then hit the notification email link again.</p><p>4) Now I'm on my profile page and it says I've got 7 new messages.&nbsp; Odd, but sure, OK.&nbsp; I hit the link to go to the PM page.</p><p>5) On that page it tells me I have one new one (which is what I expected).&nbsp; I hit the \"1 new\" link, read the PM, and everything ends up fine.</p><p>Seems to me that following a link to the site that leads directly to \"access denied\" is an experience that can be improved.&nbsp; The incorrect count of messages may be an issue.&nbsp; And of course, having some way to access PMs without needing to go through the email link is the biggest issue.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:36:01.516Z",
