        "raw": "<p>I think I read that Personal Messages are a known issue with the forums currently, but I wanted to recount my personal experience of a few minutes ago in case something can be done to improve it.</p><p>1) Nowhere on the site can I find info about any Personal Messages I may or may not have.&nbsp; I think I read that a tab should be displayed for me that&#39;s not currently being displayed, so that&#39;s a known issue.</p><p>2) I got an email on my iPhone saying that I&#39;ve got a new PM, so that&#39;s good news that notifications are working.&nbsp; Since I can&#39;t seem to get to them on my PC, I&#39;ll just hit the link in the notification email.</p><p>3) It takes me to my profile page that says &quot;access denied&quot;.&nbsp; I&#39;m not logged in on my iPhone, so I do that then hit the notification email link again.</p><p>4) Now I&#39;m on my profile page and it says I&#39;ve got 7 new messages.&nbsp; Odd, but sure, OK.&nbsp; I hit the link to go to the PM page.</p><p>5) On that page it tells me I have one new one (which is what I expected).&nbsp; I hit the &quot;1 new&quot; link, read the PM, and everything ends up fine.</p><p>Seems to me that following a link to the site that leads directly to &quot;access denied&quot; is an experience that can be improved.&nbsp; The incorrect count of messages may be an issue.&nbsp; And of course, having some way to access PMs without needing to go through the email link is the biggest issue.</p>",
